[10.2904, "o", "\r                                                \r"]
[10.2908, "o", "\u001b[38;5;208m● belay\u001b[0m\r\n  One month in, honestly — this is going well, and the data backs it up, not just the vibe.\r\n\r\n  **July closed clean.** All 18 transactions categorized automatically, nothing left for you to sort by hand, and the car insurance (€420) got caught and filed the moment it landed — no scramble. Groceries (€309) and dining (€36) landed right where the 24-month history said they would. The card refills between accounts (€454 across 4 transfers) were excluded from spending automatically, like they should be — that part just runs quietly now.\r\n\r\n  **One small thing worth naming, no action needed:** Cloudtunes is still an active charge (~€10–15/mo) — this was flagged back at onboarding as one you'd *thought* you'd cancelled. Just resurfacing it since it's still there; your call on whether it stays.\r\n\r\n  **A real win, from yesterday:** you logged deciding to wait on a €340 espresso machine — not because a limit blocked you, but because you checked it against the picture and chose to buy calm instead of on impulse. That's the awareness approach doing exactly what it's for.\r\n\r\n  No pattern yet says any category needs containing — it's one clean month, and that's the right amount of data to have right now. Nothing to propose or change. Strategy review is already scheduled for October once there's more to look at — for now, the next natural touchpoint is just letting August's actuals land and comparing them to the draft.\r\n\r\n  Good place to log off from.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;36malex ▸ \u001b[0m"]
